ities, wireless internet service providers, and broadband providers. The company was formerly known as United States Cellular Corporation and changed its name to Array Digital Infrastructure, Inc. in August 2025. The company was incorporated in 1983 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois. Array Digital Infrastructure, Inc. is a subsidiary of Telephone and Data Systems, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony J. M. Carlson | President, CEO & Director | Age 38 | Compensation: $406,692 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60 people. Revenue per employee of $2.7M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue falling 19%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $2.9M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Array Digital Infrastructure, I is a mid-cap communication services business with a $2.4B market cap on $163M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -66% over the past three years and -27% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -4.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $174M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 107 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 72% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -4.1pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 153% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5321613937589815},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 65% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Array Digital Infrastructure (AD) Could Be 31% Undervalued On Q3 Results Beat","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.s